# Heavy or regenerable. Everything here lives in the assets directory beside the arm, or
# is run output. setup_assets.py says how each piece comes back.
#
# Patterns are deliberately NOT anchored to the repo root, so this file works whether the
# arm is the repository root or nested under multi_objective/.

# Linked in by setup_assets.py: tdc resolves these relative to the process cwd
# (tdc/utils/load.py:546, tdc/chem_utils/oracle/oracle.py:346), so they must exist inside
# the tree at runtime even though they cannot be committed.
# Both forms: `oracle/` catches a real directory, the bare name catches the symlink
# setup_assets.py creates (git sees a symlink as a file, not a directory, so the
# trailing-slash form alone would let an absolute local path get committed).
oracle
oracle/
data
data/zinc.tab

# Model weights, wherever they land.
*.pkl
*.pt
*.bin
*.hdf5

# Run output: results, Pareto snapshots, discovery logs, the agent spool.
results/*
!results/.gitkeep
spool/
*.log

# Caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
property_cache.jsonl

# Environments
.venv*/
